import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Seamless vs. Cut & Sew Activewear: Which Technology Fits Your High-Volume Line?"
  description="A technical comparison for activewear brands. Explore the pros and cons of seamless knitting and traditional cut & sew manufacturing for large-scale retail."
>
  <article class="py-32 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 font-['Century_Gothic',sans-serif]">
    <header class="mb-16">
      <span class="text-accent font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">Manufacturing Tech</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mt-4 mb-8 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">Seamless vs. Cut & Sew: <span class="text-accent italic">A B2B Guide</span></h1>
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-4 text-gray-500 text-sm">
        <span>Published: June 20, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>10 Min Read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-xl text-black font-bold mb-8">Choosing the right production technology is a multi-million dollar decision. For high-volume retailers, understanding the technical tradeoffs is essential.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">1. Seamless Knitting: The High-End Choice</h2>
      <p>Seamless activewear is produced on circular knitting machines, resulting in a single tubular piece without side seams. It offers superior comfort and "naked-feel" aesthetics. For high-volume boutique brands, seamless technology is the #1 choice for leggings and sports bras due to its high perceived value and branding potential.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">2. Traditional Cut & Sew: The Versatile Workhorse</h2>
      <p>Cut & sew involves cutting fabric pieces from a roll and sewing them together. It allows for much higher complexity in patterning, multi-fabric panels, and structural reinforcement. If your brand relies on intricate panel designs, mesh inserts, or high-compression power-mesh, cut & sew remains the industry standard.</p>

      <div class="my-12 relative rounded-[40px] overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <img src="https://sc01.alicdn.com/kf/Hcc2d5570d1a94d4ea98d26ce3312893dj.png" alt="Seamless Technology" class="w-full h-auto" />
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">3. Which Technology for Your $30k Line?</h2>
      <p>For large-scale retailers in the US and EU, a balanced collection usually features 70% Cut & Sew (for core staples and complex designs) and 30% Seamless (for premium, comfort-focused "hero" items). At Fitclo, we operate high-capacity lines for both technologies, giving you the flexibility to launch complete, diversified collections under one roof.</p>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-20 pt-10 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div class="bg-black text-white p-12 rounded-[40px] text-center">
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mb-6">Master Your Technical Line</h3>
        <p class="mb-8 text-white/70">Consult with our production director to determine the best technology for your specific designs.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-accent text-black px-10 py-4 rounded-full font-black uppercase tracking-widest hover:scale-105 transition-transform">Consult Technical Director</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
